  "rules": [
    "Correct for severe downward bias: The model consistently overestimates prices during the initial 10-15 day horizon following a price drop, failing to capture the depth of the crash (e.g., forecasting ~77 while true prices fall to ~67).",
    "Adjust for delayed mean reversion: The model exhibits excessive inertia, predicting a slow, linear recovery that lags the actual sharp V-shaped rebound observed in the true outcomes (e.g., missing the spike to 80+ in the final 10 days).",
    "Ignore low sentiment signals: Positive sentiment scores (0.20-0.33) in the history do not trigger upward adjustments in the forecast; the model remains anchored to recent lows regardless of sentiment shifts.",
    "Reduce forecast horizon length: The 30-day linear projection is structurally flawed for this volatile regime; forecasts should be truncated or dynamically adjusted to reflect the high probability of a sharp reversal rather than a gradual drift."
  ]
}
